                        



Item #:  SCP-5446

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5446 is to be kept on the campus of site-██ at all times. SCP-5446 is capable and allowed to roam the facility but is to be immediately returned to her containment room if there is any sign of activity that can or has triggered a containment breach. At any given time only level 1 and higher personnel are permitted to interact with SCP-5446, level-0 personnel who interact with SCP-5446 are to be given class A amnestics. SCP-5446 is not to be let within a 30 meter vicinity of SCP-173’s containment cell at any given time without explicit permission and escortation from Dr.████████. Mentioning, talking about, and/or showing anything related to SCP-173 to SCP-5446 is strictly forbidden.

Description:  SCP-5446 or ‘Alex’ appears to be a teenage ███████████ female aged around 14-17, SCP-5446’s appearance is normal from the neck down, but her face appears to be ‘censored’ within all forms of visual contact, this includes through the naked eye and through any sort of photography or videography.

SCP-5446’s face has been reported to vary from person to person, in testing most report seeing a black square covering her face and head, but a few instead see pixilation censoring. The censor seems to be 2d, it will appear at any position around her head depending on the angle of which the observer is looking.

When asked to look into a mirror SCP-5446 just said “Yeah? It’s my face, no different from yours or his.” This could have implied that either the censor doesn’t show up in her vision, or that in her view everyone’s face is censored in this way, though the latter was proved wrong in a test where SCP-5446 was asked to describe the facial features of D-███.

Addendum:  During test ███, SCP-5446 was given a mirror and asked to describe her own facial features, hair color, and eye color. It was reported that everyone who heard her answer this question, through audio recording or through other means; died instantly. Through autopsy the cause of death was determined to be intense head trauma that seemed to leave marks around the inside and outside of the skull while leaving the outer layers of flesh untouched. During test ███, when the tester, Dr.██████; died, SCP-5446 had repeatedly asked her to wake up before sitting in the corner seeming to cry.

At a later date, during test ███, D-████ was asked to touch SCP-5446’s face and describe what he could of her facial features, Dr.████ left the room leaving SCP-5446 with D-████ and D-████. █ minutes and 29 seconds after D-████ started to describe what he felt both him and D-████ died, after this incident SCP-5446 had an alleged panic attack and refused to comply with testing for █ weeks.

The conclusion from both of these tests shows that SCP-5446 is mostly safe, and seems to have panic attacks or extreme paranoia whenever in view of any sort of corpse or things affiliated with corpses, such as blood or bones. Because of this factor, Dr.████████ deemed SCP-5446 to be allowed to roam the facility, saying that she “has human morals.”

It was discovered that some known entities are unable to perceive when SCP-5446 is looking at them, this was discovered during test ██3 where SCP-5446 was introduced to SCP-173 through live video feed. ██ seconds after Dr.████████ and the containment team looked away from SCP-173, SCP-5446 screamed and left the room, immediately locking herself in her own containment cell. It took █ months for SCP-5446 to recover from her state of intense fear, shock, and paranoia. SCP-5446 was reported to have started to talk to herself after this, usually consoling or berating herself for having “looked at that hideous thing.” SCP-5446 was introduced to a therapist soon after, she is yet to make a full recovery from this incident and due to SCP-5446’s mental state, further testing has been completely halted.







                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
